{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nDuring the comment-remediation epic, Gerrit briefly advertised `main` with parent `0fe2cc2e…` while Gitiles returned 404 for that object. Ref history appeared rewound and omitted merged commit `2a93f180…`. `git fetch gerrit main` returned timeout/HTTP 504, and CI run `34235734839` failed checkout when Gerrit returned HTTP 502 fetching change 2834. The service later recovered: the parent became readable and ref advertisement worked again.\n\nThis ticket owns the `/rebar-debug` investigation requested by the operator. RCA confirmed the actionable failure class: Verified checkout uses the pinned `checkout-gerrit-change-action`, which is mirror-first only if the GitHub mirror exposes the requested Gerrit change ref. The in-repo `infra/gerrit/replication.config` already declares `push = refs/changes/*:refs/changes/*` from ADR-0021/change 49ad69b, but the live mirror did not expose `refs/changes/34/2834/1` during the incident, so the action fell back to Gerrit and a transient Gerrit 502 failed CI before repository validation.\n\n## Operator ruling\nProceed with Option A: configure/apply Gerrit→GitHub replication so `refs/changes/*` is published to the org-private GitHub mirror, preserving the pinned checkout action's mirror-first path. Do not disturb existing `main`, `tickets`, tag, or feature-branch replication.\n\n## Plan\n- Confirm the versioned replication source includes the scoped non-meta change-ref refspec and identify whether any in-repo config change is still needed.\n- Inspect the live Gerrit replication config and compare it to `infra/gerrit/replication.config`; snapshot live config before changing host state.\n- If live config is stale, apply the repo materialized replication config through the supported setup/materializer path or an equivalent host-safe copy, preserving existing main/tag/feature refs and deploy-key materialization.\n- Reload the replication plugin if available; otherwise use the minimal restart path documented by `infra/gerrit/setup-replication.sh` only if required for the plugin to load the changed config.\n- Trigger full replication for the GitHub remote and monitor disk/CPU/log output during the initial `refs/changes/*` push spike.\n- Verify `refs/changes/*` is visible on GitHub with `git ls-remote`, spot-check an open change ref, and prove the Verified checkout path can fetch that ref from origin/GitHub without contacting Gerrit.\n- Watch the first Mirror Guard run after the change and confirm it stays green with no replication-lag alarm.\n\n## Testing\n- RED/diagnostic: before applying host config, `git ls-remote https://github.com/navapbc/rebar refs/changes/34/2834/1` showed no mirrored change ref while Gerrit had the change and the failed CI log showed Gerrit fallback HTTP 502.\n- GREEN operational: after applying, `git ls-remote https://github.com/navapbc/rebar refs/changes/*` returns change refs, an open change ref resolves, and a local CI-style `git fetch origin <refs/changes/...>` succeeds from GitHub with the Gerrit remote disabled/not contacted.\n- Repository validation: if code/config changes are required, run targeted config/workflow tests and final `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` with ambient GIT_CONFIG_* variables unset. If no repo diff is required, record the host-state verification evidence instead.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The incident timeline is supported by exact Gerrit and CI evidence.\n- [ ] A proven repo-remediable root cause explains the checkout 502/504: live GitHub replication lacked the `refs/changes/*` mirror path the pinned action expects, forcing Gerrit fallback.\n- [ ] Gerrit→GitHub replication publishes `refs/changes/*` without disturbing main/tickets/tag/feature replication or refs/meta/config privacy.\n- [ ] `refs/changes/*` visibility and a CI-style origin fetch are verified from the GitHub mirror without contacting Gerrit.\n- [ ] Mirror Guard remains green after the change and no replication-lag alarm is observed."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788929190051914001,"uuid":"c95af3ef-18e7-47d4-bec9-66047062a8fc"}